  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3\\times 5}(R))=3\\cdot 5=15.\\,\u2713\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{15}[t])=15+1=16\\ne 15.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{15})=15.\\,\u2713\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
